# Tasks: DONE-PROOF

Purpose:
  Define the Done Proof template that every task MUST produce before
  being marked COMPLETED. AI cannot simply claim "task completed" —
  it must provide evidence across five dimensions. Distinguishes
  Functional Done (code works) from Engineering Done (code works +
  tests pass + architecture valid + rules respected + documentation
  exists + review complete).

Owns:
  Done Proof template
  Functional Done vs Engineering Done
  Completion evidence requirements

DoneProofTemplate:

  TASK-<ID> DONE PROOF

  requirements:
    <description>  ✓ / ✗
  tests:
    unit:         ✓ / ✗
    integration:  ✓ / ✗
    BDD:          ✓ / ✗
  architecture:
    boundary_valid: ✓ / ✗
  review:
    no_critical_violations: ✓ / ✗
  documentation:
    generated: ✓ / ✗

  Example:
    TASK-1023 DONE PROOF

    requirements:
      refund created           ✓
      duplicate refund blocked ✓
      transaction atomic       ✓
      API response updated     ✓
    tests:
      unit:        ✓
      integration: ✓
      BDD:         ✓
    architecture:
      boundary_valid: ✓
    review:
      no_critical_violations: ✓
    documentation:
      generated: ✓

FunctionalDone:

  definition: "code works" — the feature behaves as described
  indicators:
    - manual demonstration
    - happy-path test passes
    - no obvious errors in log
  limitation: This is NOT sufficient for COMPLETED state.

EngineeringDone:

  definition: code works + all quality bars met
  requirements:
    - tests pass (unit, integration, BDD)
    - architecture valid (boundaries, patterns respected)
    - review passed (no critical violations)
    - documentation generated
    - rules respected (conventions, security, constraints)
  rule: Task is only COMPLETED when Engineering Done is achieved.

DoneProofDimensions:

  1. Requirements
     check: every acceptance criterion from the task contract is satisfied
     evidence: test assertions, API responses, behavior demonstrations
     requirement: ALL ✓

  2. Tests
     check: appropriate test levels pass
     levels: unit, integration, BDD (per testing/ levels)
     requirement: ALL ✓

  3. Architecture
     check: no boundary violations, correct layer placement, no cycles
     evidence: architecture review checklist (bax REVIEWING checklists)
     requirement: ✓

  4. Review
     check: code review passed with no critical violations
     evidence: review status = PASS or PASS_WITH_WARNINGS
     requirement: no CRITICAL or BLOCKED findings
     rule: SECURITY_CRITICAL findings force BLOCKED (not PASS_WITH_WARNINGS)

  5. Documentation
     check: human-readable documentation generated
     evidence: @human-docs-gate entry created
     requirement: ✓

ReviewResults:

  PASS               — all criteria met
  PASS_WITH_WARNINGS — passed, but warnings noted (does NOT block completion
                        unless warning is security-critical)
  CHANGES_REQUIRED   — fixes must be applied, return to FIXING
  BLOCKED            — finding blocks progress
  ESCALATE           — finding requires human decision

  rule: Only PASS or PASS_WITH_WARNINGS (without security-critical items)
        allows proceeding to DOCUMENTING.

Rules:

  [DP1] AI MUST NOT mark a task COMPLETED without a Done Proof.
  [DP2] Done Proof MUST cover all 5 dimensions: requirements, tests,
        architecture, review, documentation.
  [DP3] Functional Done alone is insufficient — Engineering Done is required.
  [DP4] Any ✗ in Done Proof means the task is NOT complete.
  [DP5] Review with SECURITY_CRITICAL findings MUST block completion.
  [DP6] Done Proof is reviewed by the next gate (LEARNING / CONSOLIDATION).
  [DP7] Partial completion is handled via PARTIAL-DONE.sdd, not a
        partial Done Proof.
  [DP8] Done Proof MUST be machine-checkable where possible.
  [DP9] Each test level (unit, integration, BDD) MUST have explicit evidence.
  [DP10] Architecture validation MUST check boundary validity, not just
         "code compiles."

